;ACME 0.97
; original patterns taken from US charset of C128
; then added umlauts and accented characters

; old charset was in CBM screencode format:
; 0x00..0x1f	@abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz[£]↑←
; 0x20..0x3f	 !"#$%&'()*+,-./0123456789:;<=>?
; 0x40..0x5f	#ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ#####	(hashes are graphics characters)
; 0x60..0x7f	 ###ä#######Ä########Öö####Üü#ß#	(hashes are graphics characters)

; new charset uses ascii format and has umlauts in first 32 slots:
; 0x00..0x1f	àáâãäÄÇçèéêëìíîï ñòóôõöÖøùúûüÜßÿ	slot 0x10 is still available!
; 0x20..0x3f	 !"#$%&'()*+,-./0123456789:;<=>?	0x20 is space
; 0x40..0x5f	@ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ[\]^_
; 0x60..0x7f	`abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz{|}~□	0x7f is ignore/rubout/delete (used for the "unavailable" symbol)
; remaining iso 8859-1 characters:
; (0xa0 is non-breaking space, 0xad is soft hyphen)
;a0-bf		 ¡¢£¤¥¦§¨©ª«¬ ®¯°±²³´µ¶·¸¹º»¼½¾¿	(do we need Pound sign? Pipe? '´'?)
;a0-bf		 ¡¢£€¥Š§š©ª«¬ ®¯°±²³Žµ¶·ž¹º»ŒœŸ¿	(ISO 8859-15 variant - Euro sign?)
;c0-df		ÀÁÂÃÄÅÆÇÈÉÊËÌÍÎÏÐÑÒÓÔÕÖ×ØÙÚÛÜÝÞß
;e0-ff		àáâãäåæçèéêëìíîïðñòóôõö÷øùúûüýþÿ
; of these we support:
;c0-df		----Ä--Ç--------------Ö-----Ü--ß
;e0-ff		àáâãä--çèéêëìíîï-ñòóôõö-øùúûü--ÿ
;...see @iso_to_local at the end of this file for the mapping table.

; for quick lookups, here's the ISO-8859/1 values for german umlauts:
;	Ä	= $c4
;	Ö	= $d6
;	Ü	= $dc
;	ß	= $df
;	ä	= $e4
;	ö	= $f6
;	ü	= $fc

!if INCLUDE_CHARSET {
